WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.890 --> 00:00:03.770
This video that I'm going to play for you
is hilarious.

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:09.500
Yesterday I reported to you the latest Fox
news poll Fox, which says, 54% of the country

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:10.750
wants Trump impeached.

00:00:10.750 --> 00:00:14.160
50% wants Trump impeached and removed.

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.539
The team over at Fox and friends had some
cognitive dissonance on this one.

00:00:18.539 --> 00:00:20.949
On the one hand, they work for Fox news.

00:00:20.949 --> 00:00:25.669
They think Fox news is right about the facts,
but they also can't believe that anybody but

00:00:25.669 --> 00:00:29.199
the most extreme leftists would want Donald
Trump impeached.

00:00:29.199 --> 00:00:35.260
So here is video of Fox news host Brian Kilmeade
visibly stunned by the results.

00:00:35.260 --> 00:00:36.990
On the one hand, it's a Fox news poll.

00:00:36.990 --> 00:00:41.460
We believe Fox news polls, but the Fox news
poll says half the country wants Trump impeached

00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:42.460
and removed.

00:00:42.460 --> 00:00:43.920
How could it be if you're watching?

00:00:43.920 --> 00:00:49.690
You may notice a perplexed look on Steve Doocy
and Ainslie Earhart's faces as well.

00:00:49.690 --> 00:00:50.690
Take a look at this.

00:00:50.690 --> 00:00:52.210
Fox poll came out and I was stunned by this.

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:54.780
This is 50% of the country want the president
impeached.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:58.001
I was stunned to see that that's the number
because I thought they'd be things that were

00:00:58.001 --> 00:00:59.050
trending away.

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:03.090
Uh, although the president's approval rating
did take up in the same poll, so it's almost

00:01:03.090 --> 00:01:04.210
like a split personality.

00:01:04.210 --> 00:01:05.700
How could this be?

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:11.950
Say it ain't so, this is what it looks like
when reality simply doesn't fit into the Fox

00:01:11.950 --> 00:01:12.950
narrative.

00:01:12.950 --> 00:01:16.720
And again, I said this yesterday and I want
to say it again.

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:21.530
Different news outlets are playing coy with
the momentum saying, wow, during impeachment

00:01:21.530 --> 00:01:25.070
hearings, support for impeachment went down.

00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:27.170
Usually it's like by two or three points.

00:01:27.170 --> 00:01:30.740
These polls have a margin of error of plus
or minus three.

00:01:30.740 --> 00:01:38.130
So a three point swing arguably means nothing,
and the poll is nowhere near 50% on lots of

00:01:38.130 --> 00:01:39.390
important internals.

00:01:39.390 --> 00:01:45.000
If you look at the same Fox news poll, you
see that by a 60 to 24 margin, it is wrong

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:48.369
to ask leaders of foreign countries to investigate
rivals.

00:01:48.369 --> 00:01:49.369
That's not close.

00:01:49.369 --> 00:01:57.270
That's 60 to 24 58 to 22 Americans say presidents
typically ask foreign leaders to do this.

00:01:57.270 --> 00:01:59.409
It should be 100 versus zero.

00:01:59.409 --> 00:02:01.350
Since clearly it's not common.

00:02:01.350 --> 00:02:05.250
Trump supporters can't seem to admit that
and are trying to use that as a defense.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:10.320
52 to 36 saying Trump isn't cooperating with
the inquiry.

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:11.320
That's very clear.

00:02:11.320 --> 00:02:15.280
People understand Trump is not cooperating
here, but once again, the most important thing

00:02:15.280 --> 00:02:20.180
to remember is that these numbers include
Republicans who said in a recent poll that

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:22.730
Trump is a better president than Abraham Lincoln.

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:29.350
We should actually be shocked that only merely
50% want Trump impeached and removed.

00:02:29.350 --> 00:02:34.330
But then you think back and realize, Oh, half
of Republicans think Trump is a better president

00:02:34.330 --> 00:02:35.340
than Lincoln.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.890
Nearly two thirds of Republicans say they
would never abandon Donald Trump, no matter

00:02:38.890 --> 00:02:45.100
what he does, then we should actually recognize
the significance of merely hitting 50% support

00:02:45.100 --> 00:02:46.360
for impeachment.

00:02:46.360 --> 00:02:51.920
Despite all of those people that are completely
disconnected from the facts and defend Trump

00:02:51.920 --> 00:02:53.269
no matter what to the death.

00:02:53.269 --> 00:02:57.040
So sometimes the bubble of alternative facts
is so thick that people forget.

00:02:57.040 --> 00:02:58.850
There's a reality out there.

00:02:58.850 --> 00:03:00.180
Your narrative isn't real.

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:04.920
That's what Brian Kilmeade seems to be smacked
in the face with directly in this video.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:09.840
But if it's real enough to the people watching
Fox news, it's real enough to do serious damage

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:12.250
to the country's ability to think critically.

00:03:12.250 --> 00:03:14.180
And that's where we find ourselves today.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:20.250
Because really imagine being stunned that
half the country wants the man who is arguably

00:03:20.250 --> 00:03:24.970
the most corrupt president in the modern presidential
era removed from office for his corruption

00:03:24.970 --> 00:03:26.849
that shouldn't be stunning.

00:03:26.849 --> 00:03:30.940
And yet somehow Brian Kilmeade is stunned
by that very backwards situation that we are

00:03:30.940 --> 00:03:30.949
in.

